<title>USA: Occidental sees higher spending, output.</title>
<headline>Occidental sees higher spending, output.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Occidental Petroleum Corp president Dale Laurance told shareholders at the company's annual meeting he expects net worldwide oil production to grow 20 percent by 1998, to 350,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>Laurance noted that a significant portion of the increase would come from enhanced oil recovery projects at existing wells.</p>
<p>Also at the meeting, Chief Executive Ray Irani forecast capital spending would rise 17 percent in 1997, to $1.4 billion.</p>
